Package: recm
Type: Package
Title: Rational Error Correction Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "LJ Valencia",
      email = "leb_valencia@yahoo.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Estimation of rational error correction models, the econometric
    representation of polynomial adjustment cost behaviour described in
    Tinsley (2002) and in the FRB/US 'PAC basics' note. The cross-equation restrictions linking the
    speed of adjustment, the weights on expected future changes in the target 
    and the structural adjustment costs are imposed rather than assumed, 
    as is the growth neutrality condition. Expectations are formed either from
    VAR-driven expectations or model-consistent expectations. Estimation is
    currently available in iterative OLS.
